# @zooroyal/itv-infrastructure ships the validate-microservice-json binary that sca:itv-infrastructure
# runs. It lives in GitHub Packages rather than on npmjs.com because the ITV infrastructure schema
# travels with it and is not public, so installing it needs a token with read:packages.
#
# Deliberately no _authToken line here. npm aborts the whole install with "Failed to replace env in
# config" when a referenced variable is unset, which would break `composer install` for anyone who
# has not exported one. The token comes from the environment instead:
#
#   * locally     ~/.npmrc, see "Working on the coding standard" in README.md
#   * in Actions  actions/setup-node writes it from NODE_AUTH_TOKEN
@zooroyal:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
